  "query_preview": "..\n\nClear skies across southern Arizona with high temperatures\nexpected to be in the mid 60s to mid 70s making it a beautiful\nThanksgiving day. The upper level pattern today is driven by\na ridge building in from the west as the cut off low that moved\nsouth of Arizona yesterday continues on its southeastward track.\nThe ridge will raise daytime high temperatures to 3 to 9 \ndegrees above normal by Friday, with highs forecast to be in the\nupper 70s to low 80s. Dry conditions and above normal \ntemperatures will persist as ridging continues through early \nnext week. \n\nIn the extended forecast, a pattern change at the end of next \nweek could bring back chances for precipitation and cooler \ntemperatures. This trend will continue with the potential for \nseveral rounds of unsettled weather. Confidence in track, \ntiming, and intensity will improve as we get closer.",
